How to install JAGURS-D
June 30, 2024

[TOC]
1. Requirements
2. How to install
3. Special instructions for each platform
   3.1. K computer
4. Troubleshooting

================================================================================
1. Requirements

JAGURS-D requires the followings.

   - Fortran compiler supports Fortran 2003 standards

   - C compiler

   - GNU make

   - NetCDF C and Fortran (URL: https://www.unidata.ucar.edu/software/netcdf/)
     If you need NetCDF4 functions (i.e. single record over 4 GByte),
     more libraries (HDF5, cURL, etc...) may be required to link.

   - FFT library
      - FFW3 (URL: http://www.fftw.org/) for others
        (MKL FFTW3 interface is also okay)

   - PROJ library (URL: https://trac.osgeo.org/proj/)

   - [optional] MPI library
     If MPI parallelization is required. (MPI=ON)

Note that GMT (URL: https://www.soest.hawaii.edu/gmt/) tools are actually
essential in front-end server (not necessary in computational server) to handle
input/output files.

================================================================================
2. How to install

About the following platforms, sample makefiles "Makefile.[platform]" exist.
In other platforms, you need to make makefile for your platform based on
existing samples.

   ifx:: For Intel OneAPI
      Intel new Fortran/C++ compilers (ifx/icx), Intel MPI and MKL FFTW3 interface
      are utilized.

   gfortran: For GNU SDK (gcc and gfortran) and OpenMPI on usual Linux system

   Aurora: For the Earth simulator 4 and NEC SX-Aurora TSUBASA

   NVIDIAGPU: For NVIDIA GPU with NVIDIA HPC SDK

   AMDGPU: For AMD GPU with ROCm

   DA (obsolete):: For JAMSTEC DA system
      Intel Fortran/C++ compilers, Intel MPI and MKL FFTW3 interface are
      utilized.

Typically, you need to modify install path of each libraries.

   NETCDF: Install path of NetCDF library

   FFTW3_INCLUDE_DIR: FFTW3 include file path

   FFTW3_LIB: Arguments to link FFTW3 library
              (Typically, "-L${FFTW3_INSTALL_DIR}/lib -lfftw3")

   PROJ_DIR: Install path of PROJ library
             By default, PROJ 4 is used, but you can use PROJ 9 by
             uncommenting "PROJ9=ON" in the Makefile. See, 4.3 below.

After necessary modifications are applied, type "make -f Makefile.[platform]"
in JAGURS-D_V???? directory.

================================================================================
3. Special instructions for each platform
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.1. GPU computing

Both NVIDIA and AMD GPUs are supported.
Multi-GPU execution with MPI parallelization is available, but it provides
adequate performance only for very large cases because MPI communication
overhead becomes significant.
For typical cases, a single GPU is sufficient.

================================================================================
4. Troubleshooting
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4.1. Undefined references to "nf_*_" (i.e. nf_create_, nf_def_dim_, etc...)
     occurs and it fails in link.

Add "-lnetcdff" before "-lnetcdf" to LIBS variable in Makefile.
If you are trying to link NetCDF4, not only libnetcdf.so but also libnetcdff.so
(Fortran lapper library) have to be liked.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4.2. PROJ library is not found and it fails in execution with the message
     like "./jagurs: error while loading shared libraries: libproj.so.X:
     cannot open shared object file: No such file or directory".

Add the path to "${PROJ_DIR}/lib" to the environment variable LD_LIBRARY_PATH.
In sh/bash, add the following line into your execution script.

   export LD_LIBRARY_PATH="${LD_LIBRARY_PATH}:${PROJ_DIR}/lib"

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4.3. Support for newer versions of the PROJ library has been added.
     To enable PROJ 9, uncomment the following line in the Makefile:

   PROJ9=ON

================================================================================

